# 5. Objective Identification Standard

## Purpose

The Objective Identification Standard establishes a consistent and traceable method for uniquely identifying every System Objective within the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA).

Each identifier shall remain permanent throughout the objective's lifecycle.

---

## Identification Structure

Every System Objective identifier shall follow the structure:

SO-<Category>-<Number>

Where:

- SO = System Objective
- <Category> = Approved Objective Category Identifier
- <Number> = Sequential three-digit identifier

Example:

SO-F-001
SO-C-001
SO-P-001

---

## Approved Category Identifiers

| Identifier | Category |
|------------|----------|
| F | Functional |
| C | Coordination |
| P | Performance |
| S | Safety |
| R | Reliability |
| H | Human Interaction |
| A | Adaptability |
| M | Maintainability |
| SC | Scalability |

---

## Identification Rules

Every objective identifier shall:

- Be unique within the repository.
- Be permanent once assigned.
- Never be reused.
- Belong to one primary objective category.
- Follow the approved naming convention.

---

## Numbering Rules

Sequential numbering shall begin at 001 for each objective category.

Examples:

SO-F-001

SO-F-002

SO-C-001

SO-S-001

The identifier shall not imply engineering priority or implementation order.

---

## Reserved Identifiers

Unused identifiers may be reserved for planned objectives where justified through engineering planning.

Reserved identifiers shall not be assigned to other objectives until formally released.

---

## Identifier Changes

Objective identifiers shall not change after approval.

If an objective requires fundamental reclassification or replacement, a new identifier shall be created while preserving traceability to the previous objective.

---

## Identifier Traceability

Every identifier shall maintain traceable links to:

- Parent governing documents.
- Related objectives.
- Derived system requirements.
- Verification activities.
- Validation activities.
- Revision history.
